<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<title>KFPL Catalog Backend API Flow</title>
<style>
body{font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:#172033;line-height:1.45;margin:42px}h1{color:#1d4ed8;border-bottom:3px solid #1d4ed8;padding-bottom:10px}h2{color:#1e40af;margin-top:28px;border-bottom:1px solid #dbeafe;padding-bottom:5px}h3{color:#334155;margin-top:22px}table{border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;margin:12px 0 20px}th{background:#1e3a8a;color:#fff;text-align:left}th,td{border:1px solid #cbd5e1;padding:8px;vertical-align:top}code,pre{font-family:Consolas,monospace}pre{background:#f1f5f9;border:1px solid #cbd5e1;padding:12px;white-space:pre-wrap}blockquote{border-left:4px solid #2563eb;padding-left:14px;color:#475569}.note{background:#eff6ff;border-left:4px solid #2563eb;padding:10px}.required{color:#b91c1c;font-weight:bold}</style>
</head>
<body>
<h1>KFPL Catalog Management Backend API Flow</h1>
<p><b>Document purpose:</b> Backend API handoff for the KFPL Admin Catalog Management module.</p>
<p><b>Resource hierarchy:</b></p>
<pre>Category
  └── Subcategory
        └── Product</pre>
<p>Products must reference an existing active <code>categoryId</code> and <code>subcategoryId</code>. Category, Subcategory, and Product are separate backend resources.</p>

<h2>1. Authentication and common rules</h2>
<p>All endpoints require an authenticated admin user.</p>
<pre>Authorization: Bearer &lt;admin_access_token&gt;
Content-Type: application/json</pre>
<table><tr><th>Permission</th><th>Usage</th></tr>
<tr><td>catalog.read</td><td>List and view catalog data</td></tr>
<tr><td>catalog.create</td><td>Create categories, subcategories, and products</td></tr>
<tr><td>catalog.update</td><td>Edit catalog records</td></tr>
<tr><td>catalog.delete</td><td>Archive catalog records</td></tr></table>
<p>Use soft deletion wherever possible. Do not physically delete records that are referenced by products, orders, or reports.</p>

<h2>2. Image upload flow</h2>
<p>Images should be uploaded before creating the catalog record. The upload API returns a permanent CDN URL and storage key.</p>
<h3>Endpoint</h3>
<pre>POST /api/v1/admin/catalog/images
Content-Type: multipart/form-data</pre>
<h3>Multipart fields</h3>
<table><tr><th>Field</th><th>Required</th><th>Values</th></tr>
<tr><td>file</td><td>Yes</td><td>JPG, JPEG, PNG, or WEBP; maximum 5 MB</td></tr>
<tr><td>type</td><td>Yes</td><td>CATEGORY, SUBCATEGORY, PRODUCT</td></tr></table>
<h3>Response</h3>
<pre>{
  "success": true,
  "data": {
    "url": "https://cdn.kfpl.com/catalog/categories/dairy-123.jpg",
    "storageKey": "catalog/categories/dairy-123.jpg"
  }
}</pre>
<p>Validate file type, file size, image dimensions, and scan the file before saving it.</p>

<h2>3. Category API flow</h2>
<h3>3.1 Create category</h3>
<pre>POST /api/v1/admin/catalog/categories</pre>
<pre>{
  "name": "Dairy, Bread &amp; Eggs",
  "imageUrl": "https://cdn.kfpl.com/catalog/categories/dairy-123.jpg",
  "imageStorageKey": "catalog/categories/dairy-123.jpg",
  "description": "Fresh dairy products, bread and eggs",
  "displayOrder": 1,
  "discount": 5,
  "isActive": true
}</pre>
<table><tr><th>Field</th><th>Type</th><th>Required</th><th>Validation</th></tr>
<tr><td>name</td><td>string</td><td class="required">Yes</td><td>2–100 characters; unique</td></tr>
<tr><td>imageUrl</td><td>string</td><td class="required">Yes</td><td>Must be returned by image upload API</td></tr>
<tr><td>description</td><td>string</td><td>No</td><td>Optional category description</td></tr>
<tr><td>displayOrder</td><td>integer</td><td>No</td><td>Minimum 0; default 0</td></tr>
<tr><td>discount</td><td>number</td><td>No</td><td>0–100; default 0</td></tr>
<tr><td>isActive</td><td>boolean</td><td>No</td><td>Default true</td></tr></table>
<h3>Successful response: HTTP 201</h3>
<pre>{
  "success": true,
  "message": "Category created successfully",
  "data": {
    "id": "cat_dairy_001",
    "name": "Dairy, Bread &amp; Eggs",
    "imageUrl": "https://cdn.kfpl.com/catalog/categories/dairy-123.jpg",
    "description": "Fresh dairy products, bread and eggs",
    "displayOrder": 1,
    "discount": 5,
    "isActive": true,
    "subcategoryCount": 0,
    "productCount": 0,
    "createdAt": "2026-08-24T12:30:00Z"
  }
}</pre>
<h3>3.2 List categories</h3>
<pre>GET /api/v1/admin/catalog/categories?search=dairy&amp;isActive=true&amp;page=1&amp;limit=20</pre>
<p>Return category image, name, description, display order, discount, status, subcategory count, and product count.</p>
<h3>3.3 Get, update, and archive category</h3>
<pre>GET    /api/v1/admin/catalog/categories/:categoryId
PATCH  /api/v1/admin/catalog/categories/:categoryId
DELETE /api/v1/admin/catalog/categories/:categoryId</pre>
<p>PATCH accepts any editable category fields. DELETE should archive the category. Reject archive requests when active products exist unless the API explicitly supports cascading archive.</p>

<h2>4. Subcategory API flow</h2>
<h3>4.1 Create subcategory</h3>
<pre>POST /api/v1/admin/catalog/subcategories</pre>
<pre>{
  "categoryId": "cat_dairy_001",
  "name": "Milk",
  "imageUrl": "https://cdn.kfpl.com/catalog/subcategories/milk-001.jpg",
  "imageStorageKey": "catalog/subcategories/milk-001.jpg",
  "description": "Toned, full cream and skimmed milk",
  "displayOrder": 1,
  "discount": 3,
  "isActive": true
}</pre>
<table><tr><th>Field</th><th>Type</th><th>Required</th><th>Validation</th></tr>
<tr><td>categoryId</td><td>string</td><td class="required">Yes</td><td>Must reference an existing category</td></tr>
<tr><td>name</td><td>string</td><td class="required">Yes</td><td>Unique within the parent category</td></tr>
<tr><td>imageUrl</td><td>string</td><td class="required">Yes</td><td>Must be returned by image upload API</td></tr>
<tr><td>description</td><td>string</td><td>No</td><td>Optional description</td></tr>
<tr><td>displayOrder</td><td>integer</td><td>No</td><td>Minimum 0; default 0</td></tr>
<tr><td>discount</td><td>number</td><td>No</td><td>0–100; default 0</td></tr>
<tr><td>isActive</td><td>boolean</td><td>No</td><td>Default true</td></tr></table>
<h3>4.2 List subcategories</h3>
<pre>GET /api/v1/admin/catalog/categories/:categoryId/subcategories
GET /api/v1/admin/catalog/subcategories?categoryId=cat_dairy_001&amp;isActive=true&amp;page=1&amp;limit=20</pre>
<h3>4.3 Get, update, and archive subcategory</h3>
<pre>GET    /api/v1/admin/catalog/subcategories/:subcategoryId
PATCH  /api/v1/admin/catalog/subcategories/:subcategoryId
DELETE /api/v1/admin/catalog/subcategories/:subcategoryId</pre>

<h2>5. Product API flow</h2>
<p>Product creation is separate from Category and Subcategory creation. The frontend first loads categories, then loads subcategories after a category is selected.</p>
<h3>5.1 Create product</h3>
<pre>POST /api/v1/admin/catalog/products</pre>
<pre>{
  "productName": "Amul Taaza Milk",
  "categoryId": "cat_dairy_001",
  "subcategoryId": "sub_milk_001",
  "brand": "Amul",
  "description": "Fresh toned milk",
  "imageUrl": "https://cdn.kfpl.com/catalog/products/amul-taaza-500.jpg",
  "imageStorageKey": "catalog/products/amul-taaza-500.jpg",
  "price": 30,
  "mrp": 32,
  "quantity": 500,
  "unit": "ml",
  "stockQuantity": 50,
  "status": "ACTIVE",
  "sku": "AML-MILK-500"
}</pre>
<table><tr><th>Field</th><th>Required</th><th>Validation</th></tr>
<tr><td>productName</td><td class="required">Yes</td><td>3–150 characters</td></tr>
<tr><td>categoryId</td><td class="required">Yes</td><td>Existing active category</td></tr>
<tr><td>subcategoryId</td><td class="required">Yes</td><td>Existing active subcategory belonging to categoryId</td></tr>
<tr><td>brand</td><td>Recommended</td><td>Maximum 100 characters</td></tr>
<tr><td>description</td><td>Recommended</td><td>Product description</td></tr>
<tr><td>imageUrl</td><td class="required">Yes</td><td>Uploaded product image</td></tr>
<tr><td>price</td><td class="required">Yes</td><td>Greater than 0</td></tr>
<tr><td>mrp</td><td>Recommended</td><td>Must be greater than or equal to price</td></tr>
<tr><td>quantity</td><td class="required">Yes</td><td>Greater than 0</td></tr>
<tr><td>unit</td><td class="required">Yes</td><td>ml, g, kg, or piece</td></tr>
<tr><td>stockQuantity</td><td class="required">Yes</td><td>Integer; minimum 0</td></tr>
<tr><td>status</td><td>Recommended</td><td>ACTIVE, DRAFT, or OUT_OF_STOCK</td></tr>
<tr><td>sku</td><td>Recommended</td><td>Unique product code</td></tr></table>
<p><b>Discount rule:</b> calculate the final product discount on the server. Do not trust a discount value sent by the browser.</p>
<pre>discountPercentage = ((mrp - price) / mrp) * 100</pre>
<h3>5.2 Product listing and filters</h3>
<pre>GET /api/v1/admin/catalog/products
  ?search=milk
  &amp;categoryId=cat_dairy_001
  &amp;subcategoryId=sub_milk_001
  &amp;stockStatus=IN_STOCK
  &amp;status=ACTIVE
  &amp;page=1
  &amp;limit=20</pre>
<p>The Products page requires product image, name, category, subcategory, stock, status, and action data. The API should return these values in each product row.</p>
<h3>5.3 Get, update, and archive product</h3>
<pre>GET    /api/v1/admin/catalog/products/:productId
PATCH  /api/v1/admin/catalog/products/:productId
DELETE /api/v1/admin/catalog/products/:productId</pre>
<h3>Product response example</h3>
<pre>{
  "success": true,
  "data": {
    "id": "prod_amul_milk_001",
    "productName": "Amul Taaza Milk",
    "category": { "id": "cat_dairy_001", "name": "Dairy, Bread &amp; Eggs" },
    "subcategory": { "id": "sub_milk_001", "name": "Milk" },
    "imageUrl": "https://cdn.kfpl.com/catalog/products/amul-taaza-500.jpg",
    "brand": "Amul",
    "price": 30,
    "mrp": 32,
    "discountPercentage": 6.25,
    "quantity": 500,
    "unit": "ml",
    "stockQuantity": 50,
    "stockStatus": "IN_STOCK",
    "status": "ACTIVE",
    "sku": "AML-MILK-500"
  }
}</pre>

<h2>6. Complete frontend sequence</h2>
<h3>Create Category</h3>
<pre>1. Admin opens Categories
2. Admin enters category name, description, display order, discount and active status
3. Admin uploads mandatory category image
4. Frontend calls POST /catalog/images with type CATEGORY
5. Frontend calls POST /catalog/categories
6. Backend validates, creates category, and returns category ID
7. Frontend refreshes category list</pre>
<h3>Create Subcategory</h3>
<pre>1. Admin opens Subcategories
2. Admin selects parent category
3. Admin enters subcategory fields
4. Admin uploads mandatory subcategory image
5. Frontend calls POST /catalog/images with type SUBCATEGORY
6. Frontend calls POST /catalog/subcategories
7. Backend validates parent category and creates subcategory
8. Frontend refreshes subcategory list</pre>
<h3>Create Product</h3>
<pre>1. Admin opens Products or Add Product
2. Frontend calls GET /catalog/categories
3. Admin selects a category
4. Frontend calls GET /catalog/categories/:categoryId/subcategories
5. Admin selects a subcategory
6. Admin fills product details and uploads mandatory product image
7. Frontend calls POST /catalog/images with type PRODUCT
8. Frontend calls POST /catalog/products
9. Backend validates category/subcategory relationship and SKU
10. Backend calculates discount and creates product
11. Frontend refreshes Products listing</pre>

<h2>7. Transactions and side effects</h2>
<ul><li>Create Category: insert category and create audit log in one transaction.</li><li>Create Subcategory: verify category, insert subcategory, update category subcategory count, and create audit log.</li><li>Create Product: verify category and subcategory relationship, calculate discount, insert product, update subcategory/category product counts, and create audit log.</li><li>On archive: do not show the record in active dropdowns or active product listings.</li><li>All create, update, archive, and image-delete operations should be auditable.</li></ul>

<h2>8. Standard error responses</h2>
<pre>400 Bad Request
{
  "success": false,
  "message": "Validation failed",
  "errors": {
    "name": "Category name is required",
    "imageUrl": "Category image is required"
  }
}</pre>
<pre>409 Conflict
{
  "success": false,
  "message": "SKU already exists",
  "field": "sku"
}</pre>
<pre>401 Unauthorized
403 Forbidden
404 Resource Not Found
500 Internal Server Error</pre>

<h2>9. Recommended database tables</h2>
<pre>categories
id, name, image_url, image_storage_key, description, display_order,
discount_percent, is_active, created_by, updated_by, created_at, updated_at, deleted_at

subcategories
id, category_id, name, image_url, image_storage_key, description, display_order,
discount_percent, is_active, created_by, updated_by, created_at, updated_at, deleted_at

products
id, category_id, subcategory_id, product_name, brand, description,
image_url, image_storage_key, price, mrp, discount_percent, quantity, unit,
stock_quantity, status, sku, created_by, updated_by, created_at, updated_at, deleted_at</pre>
<p>Recommended database constraints:</p>
<pre>UNIQUE categories.name
UNIQUE (subcategories.category_id, subcategories.name)
UNIQUE products.sku
INDEX subcategories.category_id
INDEX products.category_id
INDEX products.subcategory_id
INDEX products.status</pre>
</body>
</html>
